746	\section{Synchronization}
747	\label{synchronization}
748	The FPGA supports synchronization of the sweep across multiple devices. This feature can be enabled by setting the SYNC bit in the sweep setup register (see section~\ref{reg:sweepsetup}). When enabled, the following conditions must be met:
749	\begin{itemize}
750	\item All participating devices must be connected in a loop via the trigger input and output pins. The order of the devices is not important.
751	\item All devices must use the same sweep settings with the exception of the "Port 1 stage" and "Port 2 stage" settings in the sweep setup register.
752	\item The port stages must be configured in such a way, that for each stage exactly one port is active in one device.
753	\end{itemize}
754	
755	The synchronization works by delaying sampling until the stimulus signal is present, even when generated by another device. For each sampling stage, performs the following steps:
756	\begin{itemize}
757	\item When the device is the synchronization master (SYM bit set):
758	\begin{itemize}
759	\item Set up source and 1.LO PLLs
760	\item If applicable: wait for the "resume sweep" command
761	\item Set the trigger output to high
762	\item Wait for high level on trigger input
763	\item Sample ADCs
764	\item Set the trigger output to low
765	\item Wait for low level on trigger input
766	\end{itemize}
767	\item When the device is the synchronization slave (SYM bit not set):
768	\begin{itemize}
769	\item Set 1.LO PLL
770	\item If applicable: wait for the "resume sweep" command
771	\item Wait for high level on trigger input
772	\item Set trigger output to high
773	\item Sample ADCs
774	\item Wait for low level on trigger input
775	\item Set the trigger output to low
776	\end{itemize}
777	\end{itemize}
778	
779	\end{document}

